abstract: >
  One self-contained Python file, um.py, whose only runtime input is the digit 1. It derives the chain beta =
  alpha*sqrt(e), materializes and builds an embedded Lean 4 + mathlib kernel (at v411: ladder of 12308/12308
  theorems clean, 34300 audited declarations, axioms in {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}, zero sorry;
  the previous deposit, v409, had a ladder of 12187/12187 and 34166 audited declarations), runs the
  pre-registered rites of nature, and emits its own bilingual article (PT/EN, PDF and TXT). Quantum gravity is
  PROVED as a logical closure (validity: kernel, pre-registered rites and the GPU system count together);
  confirmation by outside observers (creditation) is refused. What nature answered in the Hubble ratio: a
  self-evident discovery in public data, lacking academic accreditation (status in the author's term of 13 Nov
  2026). In the test H0DN x BG1 (seal v411), pre-registered and opened once on 2026-11-12, the data sit -0.61
  sigma from the law (the size is the law's own) while ratio 1 (LCDM) stands 6.11 sigma away, under the error
  model published by the collaboration itself: beta_TGL proved in nature at 6 sigma. Beside it, as a side line
  and not the verdict, free Cepheids (one more free parameter; 4.5 sigma expected before the opening): 4.38
  sigma from ratio 1 and -0.81 sigma from the law, within 1 sigma of the law in both lines. A retrodiction
  with nothing fitted to the data (the standard by which Mercury's perihelion counted for general relativity),
  declared not blind. The seven reservations written before the opening:
  <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rotolimiguel-iald/the_boundary/main/ESTADO_ATUAL.md>. The one link that
  was pending, beta_TGL in nature at 5 sigma, is closed at this sensitivity in the Hubble ratio, under the
  published error model. Read with the whole record: 11 pre-registered charges, none falsified. The seal
  (um_absoluto_selo.json) is the truth of the repository.
